ot only a label.","explain":"Make the technology idea visible: name the observation, source or example you used and say why it supports the claim.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner base claims on observation, fair tests and design evidence, rather than guessing from a picture alone. Keep every claim linked to what was seen, measured or tested against criteria.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the observations, properties, criteria or test steps that carry the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your record with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your evidence? If a result is uncertain, identify what would have to be observed or tested again. One deliberate, evidence-based revision is more useful than writing a longer answer. For practical technology work, follow teacher safety rules for tools, food and devices.","icon":"📖","notice":"Writing only a final label without evidence does not show technology thinking. Correct the claim, criteria use or method, not just the neatness of the diagram.","title":"Show the evidence","visual":[{"alt":"Evaluate cycle.","caption":"Safety first.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Test</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">result noted</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Improve</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">next change</text></g></svg>"}]},{"check":{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Use an intentionally incorrect claim as a comparison. Name its specific technology error, then show the corrected evidence-based claim. Supported records follow the actual observations, criteria and purpose of the task. The other choices miss a key step or use a commo